<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Non-Human Identity Assessment — {{ org_name }}</title>
<style>
/* Everything is inline. No CDN, no external font, no remote image.
   The report has to survive being emailed as an attachment and opened on a
   laptop with no network, six months from now. */
:root {
  --ink: #14181f;
  --muted: #5b6472;
  --line: #e2e6ec;
  --bg: #ffffff;
  --panel: #f7f8fa;
  --critical: #a4161a;
  --critical-bg: #fdf0f0;
  --high: #bc4b00;
  --high-bg: #fdf4ec;
  --medium: #8a6d00;
  --medium-bg: #fcf8e8;
  --low: #2f6b45;
  --low-bg: #eff6f1;
  --info: #3a5a8c;
  --info-bg: #eef3fa;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 0 80px;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--ink);
  font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}
.wrap { max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 32px; }

header.cover {
  border-bottom: 3px solid var(--ink);
  padding: 56px 0 28px;
  margin-bottom: 40px;
}
.eyebrow {
  font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 12px;
}
h1 { font-size: 32px; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 8px; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
.subtitle { font-size: 17px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 24px; }
.meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0 40px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
.meta div { margin-bottom: 4px; }
.meta strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

.demo-banner {
  background: var(--info-bg); border: 1px solid #c6d5ea; border-left: 4px solid var(--info);
  padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 13px; margin: 24px 0 0; color: #24406b;
}

h2 {
  font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .13em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 8px;
  margin: 48px 0 20px;
}
h3 { font-size: 17px; margin: 28px 0 8px; letter-spacing: -.01em; }

.verdict {
  background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 20px 24px; margin: 0 0 24px; font-size: 15.5px;
}
.verdict p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
.verdict p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

.scores { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 0 0 8px; }
.score {
  flex: 1 1 120px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 14px 16px; background: #fff;
}
.score .n { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.03em; }
.score .l {
  font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; margin-top: 6px;
}
.score.critical { background: var(--critical-bg); border-color: #f0cbcb; }
.score.critical .n { color: var(--critical); }
.score.high { background: var(--high-bg); border-color: #f2d9c2; }
.score.high .n { color: var(--high); }
.score.medium { background: var(--medium-bg); border-color: #eee2b3; }
.score.medium .n { color: var(--medium); }
.score.low { background: var(--low-bg); border-color: #cbe3d4; }
.score.low .n { color: var(--low); }

table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13.5px; margin: 12px 0 8px; }
th {
  text-align: left; font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; padding: 8px 10px;
  border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); white-space: nowrap;
}
td { padding: 9px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
td.wrap-any { word-break: break-word; }
.mono { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 12px; }

.pill {
  display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 3px;
  font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.pill.critical { background: var(--critical); color: #fff; }
.pill.high { background: var(--high); color: #fff; }
.pill.medium { background: var(--medium); color: #fff; }
.pill.low { background: var(--low); color: #fff; }
.pill.info { background: var(--info); color: #fff; }

.finding {
  border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 20px 24px; margin: 0 0 16px; background: #fff;
  page-break-inside: avoid;
}
.finding.critical { border-left: 5px solid var(--critical); }
.finding.high { border-left: 5px solid var(--high); }
.finding.medium { border-left: 5px solid var(--medium); }
.finding.low { border-left: 5px solid var(--low); }
.finding-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 4px; }
.finding-head .id { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; }
.finding h3 { margin: 6px 0 2px; font-size: 16.5px; }
.finding .identity {
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 14px;
}
.block { margin: 14px 0 0; }
.block .label {
  font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 4px;
}
.block p { margin: 0; }
.block.evidence p {
  background: var(--panel); border-radius: 4px; padding: 10px 12px;
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: #33404f;
}

.roadmap-phase { margin-bottom: 24px; }
.roadmap-phase .phase-head {
  display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.roadmap-phase h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 16px; }
.roadmap-phase .when { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }
ol.actions { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; }
ol.actions li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
ol.actions .who { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }

ul.plain { margin: 8px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
ul.plain li { margin-bottom: 7px; }

.method-grid { display: flex; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.method-col { flex: 1 1 260px; }

footer {
  margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted);
}
.empty { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; padding: 12px 0; }

@media print {
  body { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .wrap { max-width: none; padding: 0 12mm; }
  .finding, .roadmap-phase, table { page-break-inside: avoid; }
  h2 { page-break-after: avoid; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header class="cover">
  <p class="eyebrow">Security Assessment</p>
  <h1>Non-Human Identity Assessment</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">{{ org_name }} &mdash; Okta tenant</p>
  <div class="meta">
    <div><strong>Tenant</strong><br>{{ org_url }}</div>
    <div><strong>Assessment date</strong><br>{{ generated_at }}</div>
    <div><strong>Access level</strong><br>Read-only</div>
    <div><strong>Identities inventoried</strong><br>{{ inventory|length }}</div>
    <div><strong>Findings</strong><br>{{ findings|length }}</div>
  </div>
  {% if demo %}
  <div class="demo-banner">
    <strong>Demonstration report.</strong> Generated from bundled fixture data
    representing a fictional 40-person company. No real Okta tenant was
    contacted. Every domain, identifier and name in this document is synthetic.
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</header>

<!-- 1 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>1 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Executive summary</h2>

<div class="scores">
  {% for severity in ['critical', 'high', 'medium', 'low'] %}
  <div class="score {{ severity }}">
    <div class="n">{{ counts[severity] }}</div>
    <div class="l">{{ severity }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="score">
    <div class="n">{{ inventory|length }}</div>
    <div class="l">NHIs found</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="verdict">
  {% for paragraph in verdict %}<p>{{ paragraph }}</p>{% endfor %}
</div>

{% if counts['critical'] %}
<h3>Findings requiring action within 24 hours</h3>
<ul class="plain">
  {% for finding in findings if finding.severity == 'critical' %}
  <li><strong>{{ finding.identity }}</strong> &mdash; {{ finding.finding }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}

<!-- 2 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>2 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Non-human identity inventory</h2>

<p>
  Every non-human identity discovered in the tenant, grouped by type. Most
  organisations maintain an accurate list of their employees and no list at all
  of their service accounts, API tokens and machine integrations. This section
  is that list.
</p>

{% for nhi_type, items in inventory_by_type.items() %}
<h3>{{ type_labels[nhi_type] }} <span class="mono">({{ items|length }})</span></h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Identity</th>
      <th>Owner</th>
      <th>Created</th>
      <th>Last activity</th>
      <th>Privilege</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for item in items %}
    <tr>
      <td class="wrap-any"><strong>{{ item.identity }}</strong>
        {% if item.notes %}<br><span class="mono" style="color:#5b6472">{{ item.notes }}</span>{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td class="wrap-any">{{ item.owner }}</td>
      <td>{{ item.created }}</td>
      <td class="wrap-any">{{ item.last_used or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="wrap-any">{{ item.privilege or '—' }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% else %}
<p class="empty">No non-human identities were discovered.</p>
{% endfor %}

<!-- 3 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>3 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Findings</h2>

{% if not findings %}
<p class="empty">No findings.</p>
{% endif %}

{% for finding in findings %}
<div class="finding {{ finding.severity }}">
  <div class="finding-head">
    <span class="pill {{ finding.severity }}">{{ finding.severity }}</span>
    <span class="id">NHI-{{ '%03d' % loop.index }}</span>
    <span class="id">{{ finding.nhi_type_label }}</span>
  </div>
  <h3>{{ finding.finding }}</h3>
  <div class="identity">{{ finding.identity }}{% if finding.identity_id %} &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; {{ finding.identity_id }}{% endif %}</div>

  <div class="block evidence">
    <div class="label">Evidence</div>
    <p>{{ finding.evidence }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="block">
    <div class="label">Business risk</div>
    <p>{{ finding.risk }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="block">
    <div class="label">Remediation</div>
    <p>{{ finding.remediation }}</p>
  </div>
</div>
{% endfor %}

<!-- 4 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>4 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Remediation roadmap</h2>

<p>
  Sequenced by urgency rather than by effort. Items in the first phase should be
  treated as incident-adjacent: the exposure exists now and is not mitigated by
  any compensating control.
</p>

{% for phase in roadmap %}
<div class="roadmap-phase">
  <div class="phase-head">
    <span class="pill {{ phase.severity }}">{{ phase.severity }}</span>
    <h3>{{ phase.title }}</h3>
    <span class="when">{{ phase.timeframe }}</span>
  </div>
  <ol class="actions">
    {% for action in phase.actions %}
    <li>{{ action.summary }}<br><span class="who">{{ action.detail }}</span></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</div>
{% else %}
<p class="empty">No remediation actions required.</p>
{% endfor %}

<h3>Structural recommendations</h3>
<p>
  The individual findings above are symptoms. These address the conditions that
  produced them, and are what stops the same report being true again next year.
</p>
<ul class="plain">
  <li><strong>Give every non-human identity a named owning team.</strong> The
      recurring feature of the findings in this report is not excessive
      privilege — it is absent ownership. Okta has no owner field for tokens,
      hooks or service apps, so this must be maintained deliberately, in a naming
      convention or an external register.</li>
  <li><strong>Add credential revocation to offboarding.</strong> Deactivating a
      user does not revoke the API tokens they created, and those tokens keep
      their original privileges. Offboarding should explicitly check for tokens,
      hooks and service accounts associated with the departing person.</li>
  <li><strong>Prefer API service integrations over static API tokens.</strong>
      This is Okta's own guidance. Scoped OAuth credentials can be granted narrow
      permissions and reasoned about; a static API token silently inherits
      whatever its creator had.</li>
  <li><strong>Include non-human identities in access reviews.</strong> Quarterly
      reviews almost always cover employees only. Service accounts and
      integrations accumulate precisely because nothing forces anyone to
      re-justify them.</li>
</ul>

<!-- 5 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>5 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Methodology, scope and limitations</h2>

<div class="method-grid">
  <div class="method-col">
    <h3>What was examined</h3>
    <ul class="plain">
      {% for item in scope_covered %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="method-col">
    <h3>What was not examined</h3>
    <ul class="plain">
      {% for item in scope_excluded %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Access and method</h3>
<p>
  This assessment was performed with read-only API access to the Okta tenant.
  The tool used issues HTTP GET requests exclusively; no create, update or delete
  operation exists anywhere in its codebase. No configuration was changed, no
  credential was rotated, and no user was notified. Destination endpoints
  referenced by hooks were catalogued from configuration and were
  <em>not</em> contacted &mdash; probing a client's third-party endpoints is a
  side effect an audit should not have.
</p>

<h3>Severity definitions</h3>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Severity</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for severity in ['critical', 'high', 'medium', 'low'] %}
    <tr>
      <td><span class="pill {{ severity }}">{{ severity }}</span></td>
      <td>{{ severity_definitions[severity] }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Limitations</h3>
<ul class="plain">
  <li><strong>Service-account detection is probabilistic.</strong> Okta has no
      field marking an account as non-human. Accounts were scored against four
      signals &mdash; naming convention, absence of enrolled MFA, absence of
      interactive sign-in, and presence of API activity &mdash; and reported
      above a threshold of {{ threshold }}. Shared human accounts (a team
      mailbox, a training login) can score highly and be false positives. A
      machine identity named like a person, or one whose credential a human
      occasionally uses in a browser, will be missed. Each finding lists the
      signals it matched so individual determinations can be contested.</li>
  <li><strong>Activity signals depend on System Log retention.</strong>
      "No interactive sign-in" means none within the retained log window, not
      none ever.</li>
  {% for limitation in scope_limitations %}
  <li>{{ limitation }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
  <li><strong>Point-in-time.</strong> This reflects tenant configuration as of
      {{ generated_at }}. It is not a continuous control.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Suggested next scope</h3>
<p>
  Non-human identity does not stop at the identity provider. The categories
  excluded above &mdash; credentials in CI/CD systems, cloud IAM roles and access
  keys, secrets committed to source control, and API keys held directly inside
  SaaS applications &mdash; typically outnumber those in Okta by a wide margin
  and are subject to the same absence of ownership. Extending the inventory to
  those systems is the natural follow-on to this engagement.
</p>

<footer>
  Generated by <strong>okta-nhi-audit-tool</strong> &mdash; read-only Okta
  non-human identity assessment.<br>
  {{ generated_at }}{% if demo %} &middot; demonstration data{% endif %}
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
